international partners. Ethiopia is landlocked, but, according to Hussein, is fully dependent on the Red Sea for maritime trade. The Bab el-Mandeb Strait connects the Red Sea with the Gulf of Aden and is an important route for vessels traveling between Asia, the Suez Canal, and Europe. More current news is available on the UA.News Telegram channel Telegram . Participants’ positions and dispute with Eritrea UN Secretary-General’s Special Envoy for the Horn of Africa Guang Cong described the situation in the region as a polycrisis. According to him, the wars in Sudan, South Sudan, and Somalia, as well as threats to shipping in the Red Sea, are closely interconnected. The envoys of Germany and France also stressed the need to strengthen multilateral cooperation and support peace initiatives led by countries in the region, as well as economic integration. During the discussion, Ethiopian Prime Minister’s adviser for East Africa Getachew Reda said that Eritrea continues actions that fuel the crisis. Earlier, Eritrea’s Ministry of Foreign Affairs rejected Addis Ababa’s accusations that Eritrean troops had crossed into Ethiopian territory. Read us on Download our app RELATED MATERIALS News Around the World 31.7% of residents under 24 in Goseong County have migrant backgrounds — Korea Herald News Around the World Study reveals colonial roots of Australia's wildfire vulnerability — Mongabay News Around the World YBS in Sinjar are to disarm and join Iraq’s security forces — Anadolu Agency News Around the World Israel sets up training polling station for people with disabilities — Jerusalem Post News Around the World Saudi Arabia and Greece to strengthen defense cooperation — Asharq Al-Awsat News Around the World ATSB: Controller with fatigue risk was on duty during aircraft close calls in Sydney — ABC News Australia News Around the World Stepfather detained in Argentina after 10-year-old girl found pregnant — NDTV × World Ukraine Kyiv Polytics Business Technologies Sport proL